From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:26:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 33/48] net: xpon: omci: upload a frozen MIB snapshot and split
 large MEs

G.988 MIB upload: the ONU takes a snapshot of its MIB, answers with the
number of MIB upload next commands needed to read it, and serves each of
them from the snapshot. An ME whose attributes do not fit the 26 bytes
of one MIB upload next response is sent in several, each with its own
part of the attribute mask.

The agent announced one command per ME and encoded each ME on the fly
from the live MIB, stopping at the first attribute that did not fit, so
those attributes never reached the OLT: the circuit pack vendor ID,
equipment ID and T-CONT, priority queue and traffic scheduler counts,
the cardholder actual equipment ID, the VEIP TCP/UDP pointer and IANA
port, the 802.1p mapper DSCP to P-bit mapping, default P-bit and TP type,
and so on. MEs without a descriptor went out as 26 raw bytes under an
attribute mask of 0xffff, claiming attributes ONU-G and ONU2-G do not
have.

Build the snapshot when MIB upload arrives, splitting each ME into as
many records as its attributes need, and answer MIB upload next from it.
Drop it on MIB reset, when the OMCC channel changes and when the ONU
identity changes. The first record of every ME is the one the agent sent
before; checked in userspace for every ME class.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
